course: dictionary
lesson: 13749
title: Temporary words: interim
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you that something is not final. It is only for now, until something better or permanent comes along. «The school has an interim head teacher until a new one starts in May.» The clue is until. An interim head teacher is in charge for now, but not forever.
explain: Interim can also mean the time in between two things. «The trains stopped. In the interim, we waited in the café.» The clue is in the interim, which means while we were waiting for the trains to start again. Meanwhile is a good swap: "Meanwhile, we waited in the café" still makes sense.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If "for now" or "meanwhile" fits, you are right. If "forever" fits, you are wrong, because interim is never forever.
fact: Interim means for the time being, until something permanent is arranged.
fact: In the interim means in the time between two events; meanwhile.
fact: «An interim report» is a report sent before the final one, so it is temporary.
fact: Interim is a formal word, often used in news and official writing.
fact: Clue words like until, for now and meanwhile help you find the meaning of interim.
exercise: «The school has an interim head teacher until a new one starts in May.» What does interim mean here? | Permanent and forever | Loud and cheerful | *Temporary, just until a permanent one is found | Very old
exercise: The school sent home an interim report in January. What kind of report is it? | A report with no words | The final report of the year | A report about the weather | *A temporary report, before the final one
exercise: «The trains stopped. In the interim, we waited in the café.» What does in the interim mean? | *Meanwhile, in the time between two events | Instead of going home | Long ago | After the very end of the day
test: «The painter used an interim design until the final picture was ready.» What does interim mean? | Forever | Very cheerful | Hidden under a cloth | *Temporary, until something permanent is ready
test: Which phrase means "meanwhile"? | By the sea | At the very end | *In the interim | Once upon a time
exam: Which sentence uses interim correctly? | We swam interim every Sunday forever. | The apple was interim red and round. | *The shop is closed for an interim repair, so we use the one down the road. | My interim shoes are the biggest in the class.
